{title: Who Is My Neighbor}
{subtitle: Luke 10:25–37}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | ×10

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
An expert in the [Gm]law stood up
To [Eb]test [Bb]him in the crowd
Teacher, what must [F]I do to live
He asked the [Bb]question loud
Love God [Gm]with all your [Eb]heart and soul
Your neighbor as [Bb]yourself
But who [Gm]then is my neigh[F]bor, sir
He asked, [Bb]to clear himself
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Who [Eb]is my neighbor
Who [F]will stop along the road
The one who [Bb]showed him [F/A]mercy
[Gm]Go and do like[Eb]wise
[F]Go and do like[Bb]wise
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A man went down to Jericho
And [Gm]robbers struck him [Eb]down
They [Bb]stripped him and they beat him there
And left [F]him on the ground
A [Gm]priest came by and saw him lie
And [Eb]passed the other side
A [Bb]Levite came [Gm]and did the same
[F]And left him there to [Bb]die
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
But a Sa[Gm]maritan drew near
And [Eb]saw him where he [Bb]lay
And he was moved with compassion
He [F]would not turn away
He [Gm]bound his wounds with oil and wine
He [Eb]set him on his own
And [Bb]brought him to an [Gm]inn and stayed
And [F]did not leave him [Bb]alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Who is [Eb]my neighbor
Who [F]will stop along the road
The one who [Bb]showed him [F/A]mercy
[Gm]Go and do like[Eb]wise
[F]Go and do like[Bb]wise
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
